IMPORT `da-vehicles`

-- Duties Act 2008 (WA), Chapter 5, ss 229, 230, 232, 236 -- worked cases, from the seat of the buyer.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case, a Revenue WA ruling or calculator, or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table (scratchpad gen_wa_duties-act-2008_baseline.py). Expected results were written by hand from the text.

§ `ss 229, 230, 232 -- who pays`

#ASSERT `Must I pay vehicle licence duty` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I pay vehicle licence duty` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

§ `s 236 -- the amount (c074)`

-- s 236(2)(b): R = 2.75 + [(DV - 25000) / 6666.66], rounded to 2 decimal places (mrdoc_49812.formulas.md).
-- c074 (2034-06-15): a $28,000 used car. R = 2.75 + 3000 / 6666.66 = 3.2000.. -> 3.20, so $896, not the life's $770
-- (a flat 2.75%, which the text allows only up to $25,000).
#ASSERT `What vehicle licence duty must I pay` 28000 FALSE EQUALS 896
#ASSERT `What vehicle licence duty must I pay` 25000 FALSE EQUALS 687.5
#ASSERT `What vehicle licence duty must I pay` 30000 FALSE EQUALS 1050
#ASSERT `What vehicle licence duty must I pay` 37500 FALSE EQUALS 1736.25
#ASSERT `What vehicle licence duty must I pay` 50000 FALSE EQUALS 3250
#ASSERT `What vehicle licence duty must I pay` 12345 FALSE EQUALS 339.45
#ASSERT `What vehicle licence duty must I pay` 50001 FALSE EQUALS 3250.05
#ASSERT `What vehicle licence duty must I pay` 100000 TRUE EQUALS 3000
#ASSERT `What vehicle licence duty must I pay` 500000 TRUE EQUALS 12000

